[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":901,"buildId":902},["ShallowReactive",2],{"\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup":3,"\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup-surround":375,"navigation":386},{"id":4,"title":5,"authors":6,"badge":12,"body":13,"date":361,"description":362,"extension":363,"image":364,"meta":365,"navigation":370,"path":371,"seo":372,"stem":373,"__hash__":374},"posts\u002F3.blog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup.md","My New Home Office Setup",[7],{"name":8,"to":9,"avatar":10},"Alexander Trost","https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fgalexrt",{"src":11},"\u002Fimages\u002Fprofile-picture.webp",null,{"type":14,"value":15,"toc":343},"minimark",[16,20,25,28,31,35,40,43,65,68,77,81,84,87,110,113,117,120,123,127,140,143,179,182,186,195,204,207,210,227,231,234,278,281,285,294,297,301,310,314,317,324,330,333,337,340],[17,18,19],"p",{},"In this post I'm going over my new game and home office setup.",[21,22,24],"h2",{"id":23},"new-table","New table",[17,26,27],{},"First part of the new home setup, was a new table.\nThe previous was a cheap table from IKEA. The new table is 2.60m long instead of previously only 2.00m.\nThe 0.60m more space is awesome. The desk feels emptier but in a good way, and I have more space for equipment.",[17,29,30],{},"If you have the space, go for a big table and keep it clean!",[21,32,34],{"id":33},"tech-stuff","Tech stuff",[36,37,39],"h3",{"id":38},"power-distribution","Power Distribution",[17,41,42],{},"The following power strips are used for power distribution:",[44,45,46,57],"ul",{},[47,48,49,50],"li",{},"2x ",[51,52,56],"a",{"href":53,"rel":54},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fintl\u002Fadam_hall_874716_power_strip_1_u_19.htm",[55],"nofollow","Adam Hall 874716 Power Strip 1 U 19\" - 16-port",[47,58,59,60],{},"And some ",[51,61,64],{"href":62,"rel":63},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fintl\u002Fthe_t_racks_power_8_s.htm",[55],"the t.racks Power 8 S - 8-port",[17,66,67],{},"The 16-port power strips are pretyy neat and I can recommend them.\n(I'll soon \"mount\" them to the table so that the cables are off the ground)",[17,69,70,71,76],{},"End goal here would be to finally buy myself a fancy ",[51,72,75],{"href":73,"rel":74},"https:\u002F\u002Fen.wikipedia.org\u002Fwiki\u002FUninterruptible_power_supply",[55],"Uninterruptible power supply",", just in case the apocalypse is happening :-D",[36,78,80],{"id":79},"network","Network",[17,82,83],{},"I'm driving a dual WAN setup using a FritzBoxes and a OpenSense firewall router.",[17,85,86],{},"OpenSense firewall router box hardware specifications:",[44,88,89,92,95,98,101,104,107],{},[47,90,91],{},"CPU: Intel Celeron G4900",[47,93,94],{},"Fan: Noctua NH-L9x65 CPU-Kühler",[47,96,97],{},"RAM: Crucial Ballistix DDR4-2666 4GB",[47,99,100],{},"Mainboard: Gigabyte B360N WIFI",[47,102,103],{},"PSU: Kolink SFX-350",[47,105,106],{},"Sorage: Samsung 860 EVO 260GB SSD",[47,108,109],{},"Case: Kolink - Satellite Mini-ITX-\u002F Micro-ATX-Gehäuse - schwarz",[17,111,112],{},"For network switches, I'm using two cheap 8-port Netgear Managed Switches which get the job done (they can VLAN so perfect with my OpenSense firewall router).",[36,114,116],{"id":115},"automation","Automation",[17,118,119],{},"I have a few Raspberry Pis which power the video surveillance and security system, and take care of home automations, like turning on the lights in the morning and so on.",[17,121,122],{},"I can probably extend this, but I'm fine with what it does right now.",[36,124,126],{"id":125},"computers","Computers",[128,129,130,137],"blockquote",{},[17,131,132,133,136],{},"The most important part of the calculation are the ",[134,135,125],"del",{}," calculators.",[17,138,139],{},"- Alexander Trost",[17,141,142],{},"I have two machines, one for gaming and one for working:",[44,144,145,162],{},[47,146,147,148],{},"Gaming\n",[44,149,150,153,156,159],{},[47,151,152],{},"CPU: Intel(c) I7-7700k",[47,154,155],{},"Memory: 16GB DDR4-3000",[47,157,158],{},"GPU: Nvidia GeForce GTX 970",[47,160,161],{},"Disk(s): 1x 500GB SATA SSD, 1x 3TB SATA HDD, 1x 4TB SATA HDD",[47,163,164,165],{},"Workstation\n",[44,166,167,170,173,176],{},[47,168,169],{},"CPU: AMD Ryzen 7 1800X",[47,171,172],{},"Memory: 32GB DDR4-2133",[47,174,175],{},"GPU: 2x Radeon RX 560 OC 4G",[47,177,178],{},"Disk(s): 1x 500GB NVMe SSD, 1x 500GB SATA SSD",[17,180,181],{},"Obviously the gaming computer can always need an upgrade but I am happy with it and the workstation.\nYou really notice the 8 cores and 16 threads of the AMD Ryzen when compiling code.",[36,183,185],{"id":184},"monitors","Monitors",[17,187,188,189,194],{},"I'm currently using 4x LG 29UM68-P 29\" 21:9 UltraWide LED monitors, see ",[51,190,193],{"href":191,"rel":192},"http:\u002F\u002Fwww.lg.com\u002Fus\u002Fmonitors\u002Flg-29UM68-P-ultrawide-monitor",[55],"LG 29UM68-P 29\" product page",".",[17,196,197,198,203],{},"A big shoutout to ",[51,199,202],{"href":200,"rel":201},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002F",[55],"Ricoo Medientechnik"," for their awesome and not too expensive* monitor stands!",[17,205,206],{},"(*In comparsion with around 4 other companies that sell and\u002F or buy monitor stands)",[17,208,209],{},"I'm using the following monitor stands from Ricoo:",[44,211,212,220],{},[47,213,214,215],{},"1x ",[51,216,219],{"href":217,"rel":218},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002Fen\u002Fricoo-pc-screen-led-monitor-stand-ts3511-table-mount-for-2-monitors-monitor-brackets-tft-swivel-arm-monitor-mount-pivoting-monitor-fastener-monitor-rack-monitor-arm-compatible-with-vesa-100x100\u002Fa-11189\u002F",[55],"Ricoo Monitor Stand TS3511 Table Mount for 2 Monitors (TS3011)",[47,221,49,222],{},[51,223,226],{"href":224,"rel":225},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002Fen\u002Fricoo-desk-mount-monitor-ts3011-with-gas-spring-articulation-monitor-bracket-swivelling-tiltable-desk-monitor-stand-pedestal-flat-screen-pc-monitor-tft-display-swivel-arm-desk-led-lcd-desk-holder-brackets-universal-tv-vesa-75x75-100x100\u002Fa-10789\u002F",[55],"Ricoo Desk Monitor Mount Arm (TS3011)",[36,228,230],{"id":229},"audio","Audio",[17,232,233],{},"Moving on to the audio equipment, I use the following pieces for audio input and output control:",[44,235,236,250,257,270],{},[47,237,238,243,244,249],{},[51,239,242],{"href":240,"rel":241},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fde\u002Fdbx_286_s.htm",[55],"DBX 286 S"," (Temporarily switched out for ",[51,245,248],{"href":246,"rel":247},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fgb\u002Fbehringer_xenyx_802.htm",[55],"Behringer 802 Xenyx",")",[47,251,252],{},[51,253,256],{"href":254,"rel":255},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fde\u002Frode_nt1a_complete_vocal_recording.htm",[55],"Rode NT1-A Complete Vocal Recording",[47,258,259,264,265,249],{},[51,260,263],{"href":261,"rel":262},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fgb\u002Fnumark_m_4_black.htm",[55],"Numark M 4"," (The link is to the black edition, but I have the grey one. I got it cheap from ",[51,266,269],{"href":267,"rel":268},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.rockshop.de\u002F",[55],"Rockshop.de",[47,271,272,277],{},[51,273,276],{"href":274,"rel":275},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.rockshop.de\u002Fakai-mpx8",[55],"Akai MPX8"," (Just for the lolz as a soundboard style \"player\")",[17,279,280],{},"To \"blast\" music at the neighbors I have a very old 5.1 sound system, which sadly has a high level of noise by default. I'll probably replace it soon with a better sound system.",[36,282,284],{"id":283},"chair","Chair",[17,286,287,288,293],{},"A ",[51,289,292],{"href":290,"rel":291},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.caseking.de\u002Fnoblechairs-epic-gaming-stuhl-schwarz-gold-gagc-038.html",[55],"noblechairs EPIC Gaming Stuhl - schwarz\u002Fgold"," because your arse and back will thank you for it.",[17,295,296],{},"Pretty good chair, though if you want to spend more go for a more expensive one with, e.g., \"limitless\" backrest and more features.",[21,298,300],{"id":299},"finishing-touches","Finishing touches",[17,302,303,304,309],{},"To give the whole setup a nice touch, I have added ",[51,305,308],{"href":306,"rel":307},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.amazon.de\u002FPhilips-LightStrip-erweiterbar-Millionen-kompatibel\u002Fdp\u002FB0148NMVQA",[55],"Philipps Hue LED Lightstrips"," to the back of the monitors. Though I still have to finally use the \"in-built\" glue of the light strips to put them on the back of the monitors.",[21,311,313],{"id":312},"result","Result",[17,315,316],{},"The result is pretty rad!",[17,318,319],{},[320,321],"img",{"alt":322,"src":323},"My New Home Setup - Rad Results!","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup\u002Fhomeoffice-desktop-setup-shot-1.jpg",[17,325,326],{},[320,327],{"alt":328,"src":329},"My New Home Setup - With colored background lighting even better!","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup\u002Fhomeoffice-desktop-setup-shot-2.jpg",[17,331,332],{},"(The LightStrip is hanging down as this was a picture during me gluing it to the monitors with the integrated glue strips)",[21,334,336],{"id":335},"summary","Summary",[17,338,339],{},"That is my home office setup. It gets the job done and is a dream come true for me.\nI have more ideas to exapnd this setup, e.g., making cut outs for the mixer, but I have to see if I'm going that far.",[17,341,342],{},"Have Fun!",{"title":344,"searchDepth":345,"depth":345,"links":346},"",2,[347,348,358,359,360],{"id":23,"depth":345,"text":24},{"id":33,"depth":345,"text":34,"children":349},[350,352,353,354,355,356,357],{"id":38,"depth":351,"text":39},3,{"id":79,"depth":351,"text":80},{"id":115,"depth":351,"text":116},{"id":125,"depth":351,"text":126},{"id":184,"depth":351,"text":185},{"id":229,"depth":351,"text":230},{"id":283,"depth":351,"text":284},{"id":299,"depth":345,"text":300},{"id":312,"depth":345,"text":313},{"id":335,"depth":345,"text":336},"2018-06-05T13:47:13+02:00","In this post I'm showing you my new gaming and home office setup.","md",{"src":323},{"tags":366},[367,368,369,126],"Home","Offi